# Code owners for composemux.
#
# This file is one half of the "a human maintainer must approve" guard; the
# other half is the "Require review from Code Owners" rule on the protected
# branch. Neither works alone: without the rule this file only requests
# reviews, and without this file the rule has nobody to require.
#
# It also closes a specific gap. Automated reviewers can submit an APPROVED
# review, and a plain "require N approvals" rule counts it — so a bot alone can
# satisfy the check. GitHub Apps cannot be listed as code owners, so requiring
# a code owner's approval means a person has to sign off.
#
# Two rules for anything added below:
#
#   1. Only accounts with write access count. Listing a read-only account
#      silently does nothing.
#   2. Humans only — either individuals or teams of humans. Never add a bot or an automation account, even one the
#      project controls -- that hands the human approval back to a machine and
#      reopens the gap this file exists to close.
#
# When there is more than one maintainer, prefer a team over individuals
# (`* @sofired/maintainers`), so people can be added or removed without a
# commit here.

* @scottescue
